WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.281 --> 00:00:08.836
An hour before sunset in October 1815, a man traveling on foot entered a little town in France.

2
00:00:08.838 --> 00:00:15.195
The few people who were at their windows at that hour nervously watched this wretched-looking traveler.

3
00:00:15.196 --> 00:00:25.504
He wore a coarse yellow shirt, blue trousers with holes in the knees, and a ragged, gray smock that was patched with green cloth sewed with twine.

4
00:00:25.505 --> 00:00:28.933
His hair was short and his beard was long.

5
00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:37.321
He appeared to be in his mid-forties, although it was difficult to tell because a leather cap hid part of his sweaty, dusty face.

6
00:00:37.322 --> 00:00:42.663
The man must have been walking all day because he appeared very weary.

7
00:00:42.664 --> 00:00:51.171
When he reached the center of town, he walked toward the mayor’s office. He went in and fifteen minutes later, he came out.

8
00:00:51.172 --> 00:01:00.219
The stranger made his way toward the inn and entered the kitchen. The innkeeper was busy preparing a huge dinner in the fireplace.

9
00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:07.631
Hearing the door open and a newcomer enter, the innkeeper asked, without raising his eyes, "What does monsieur want?"

10
00:01:07.632 --> 00:01:10.241
"Something to eat and a place to stay."

11
00:01:10.242 --> 00:01:18.464
"Nothing is easier." The innkeeper looked up and started to smile, but then he saw his ragged guest. "For pay."

12
00:01:18.465 --> 00:01:22.934
The man drew a large leather purse from his pocket. "I have money."

13
00:01:22.935 --> 00:01:25.552
"Then I am at your service. Have a seat."

14
00:01:25.553 --> 00:01:31.274
While the stranger waited for his dinner, the innkeeper scribbled a note and handed it to a boy.

15
00:01:31.275 --> 00:01:39.187
He whispered something to the child, who ran off. In a few minutes the boy returned and showed a scrap of paper to the innkeeper.

16
00:01:39.188 --> 00:01:43.457
The innkeeper went over to the stranger, who was sitting by the fire.

17
00:01:43.458 --> 00:01:45.849
"Is dinner ready?" asked the man.

18
00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:49.941
"Get out!" the innkeeper whispered in his ear.

19
00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:59.441
"I was suspicious when you arrived so I sent a message to the mayor’s office. I know you’re Jean Valjean and I also know what you are."

20
00:01:59.442 --> 00:02:04.758
The stranger bowed his head, picked up his knapsack, and went outside.

21
00:02:04.759 --> 00:02:12.876
He walked through the town, stopping to ask for food and lodgings at a tavern and a house, but no one would let him in.

22
00:02:12.877 --> 00:02:15.575
The weary man even tried the prison.

23
00:02:15.576 --> 00:02:22.004
"A prison isn’t a tavern," said the guard at the door. "Get yourself arrested and we’ll open the door for you."

24
00:02:22.005 --> 00:02:27.505
It was now dark, and the exhausted stranger lay on a stone bench in front of the church.

25
00:02:27.506 --> 00:02:31.147
Just then an old woman emerged from the church.

26
00:02:31.148 --> 00:02:33.742
"What are you doing?" she asked.

27
00:02:33.743 --> 00:02:37.140
"Can’t you see I’m going to sleep?" he said angrily.

28
00:02:37.141 --> 00:02:41.393
"You can’t sleep there. Have you tried the inn?"

29
00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:47.814
"I don’t have enough money for the inn," Valjean lied. "I’ve knocked on every door, and everybody has driven me away."

30
00:02:47.815 --> 00:02:56.798
The woman handed him four coins. "Take these and knock on that door over there." She pointed to a small house next to the church.

31
00:02:56.799 --> 00:03:04.044
Bishop Myriel lived there with his sister, Mademoiselle Baptistine, and their housekeeper, Madame Magloire.

32
00:03:04.045 --> 00:03:08.290
The bishop was famous for giving away most of his wealth to the poor.

33
00:03:08.291 --> 00:03:16.486
The only luxury he allowed himself was to keep some silver: a set of six plates, a ladle, and two candlesticks.

34
00:03:16.487 --> 00:03:19.123
There were no locks on his doors.

35
00:03:19.124 --> 00:03:25.528
While Madame Magloire was at the market, she heard that a dangerous man had arrived in town.

36
00:03:25.529 --> 00:03:33.099
"He’s a dangerous beggar!" she said breathlessly to Bishop Myriel as he sat before the fire with his sister.

37
00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:40.433
"Everyone is locking their doors, but we don’t have locks and you have the bad habit of saying, ‘Come in,’ even at midnight and . . ."

38
00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:48.168
She chattered on about the dangerous man, but the bishop wasn’t listening. Just then there was a violent knock at the door.

39
00:03:48.169 --> 00:03:50.345
"Come in!" said the bishop.

40
00:03:50.346 --> 00:03:56.362
The door opened wide as if pushed by someone with great strength, and the stranger entered.

41
00:03:56.363 --> 00:03:59.416
Madame Magloire didn’t dare to scream.

42
00:03:59.417 --> 00:04:06.416
Mademoiselle Baptistine sat trembling with her mouth open. Bishop Myriel looked calmly at the intruder.

43
00:04:06.417 --> 00:04:10.416
"My name is Jean Valjean and I’m a convict!" blurted out the man.

44
00:04:10.417 --> 00:04:18.392
"I spent 19 years on the prison ships. Four days ago I was set free, and I’ve walked thirty miles today. Can I stay here?"

45
00:04:18.393 --> 00:04:23.051
"Madame Magloire, set another place at the table," said the bishop.

46
00:04:23.052 --> 00:04:26.286
"Did you hear me? I’m a convict!" said Valjean.

47
00:04:26.287 --> 00:04:30.559
"Here’s my yellow identity card. That’s enough to get me kicked out wherever I go!

48
00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:38.218
It says right here: ‘This man is very dangerous.’ I must show it at the mayor’s office in every town where I spend the night."

49
00:04:38.219 --> 00:04:44.369
"Monsieur, sit down," said the bishop. "We’ll eat shortly and your bed will be made ready."

50
00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:48.448
Valjean could not believe that someone was treating him so kindly.

51
00:04:48.449 --> 00:04:53.361
He was soon eating from the silver plates with the bishop and Mademoiselle Baptistine.

52
00:04:53.362 --> 00:04:58.115
After dinner the bishop showed him to a bed near the bishop’s own bedroom.

53
00:04:58.116 --> 00:05:04.782
As they were passing through the bishop’s room, Madame Magloire was putting away the silver in the cupboard behind the bed.

54
00:05:04.783 --> 00:05:09.012
"A good night’s rest will make you feel better," said the bishop.

55
00:05:09.013 --> 00:05:17.353
"Thank you," said Valjean quietly, but then his voice turned harsh. "You let me sleep so close to you. How do you know I’m not a murderer?"

56
00:05:17.354 --> 00:05:20.766
The bishop just smiled and said, "Good night."

57
00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:26.186
Although Valjean had told the bishop that he was a convict, he hadn’t told the whole story.

58
00:05:26.187 --> 00:05:33.416
He'd been born into a poor peasant family. After he grew up, he became a tree pruner like his father.

59
00:05:33.417 --> 00:05:40.663
Valjean’s parents had died when he was very young. He had only one relative left, a sister who took him in.

60
00:05:40.664 --> 00:05:46.663
When her husband died, she had seven children ranging in age from one to eight.

61
00:05:46.664 --> 00:05:51.980
Valjean was then in his mid-twenties and took his place as head of the household.

62
00:05:51.981 --> 00:06:00.934
He earned 18 sous a day during tree-pruning season. After that season ended, he worked as a reaper, driver, or laborer.

63
00:06:00.935 --> 00:06:03.473
He did whatever work he could find.

64
00:06:03.474 --> 00:06:09.552
His sister also worked, but misery closed in on this sad family.

65
00:06:09.553 --> 00:06:16.060
There was a very severe winter. Valjean had no work, and the family had nothing to eat.

66
00:06:16.061 --> 00:06:23.965
Valjean broke into a bakery and stole a loaf of bread for the children. The baker ran after him and caught him.

67
00:06:23.966 --> 00:06:28.294
Valjean was arrested and sentenced to five years on a prison ship.

68
00:06:28.295 --> 00:06:33.941
He was dressed in a red smock, and his past life was erased, even his name.

69
00:06:33.942 --> 00:06:42.870
He was now a prisoner—Number 24601. His four escape attempts lengthened his sentence to 19 years.

70
00:06:42.871 --> 00:06:49.100
He lost track of his family, although he later heard that his sister and one child had moved to Paris.

71
00:06:49.101 --> 00:06:57.925
There was one area where Valjean excelled in prison: He was stronger than the other inmates and could lift and hold enormous weights on his back.

72
00:06:57.926 --> 00:07:07.346
Jean Valjean had walked onto the prison ship sobbing and shuddering, but he left it hardened physically, mentally, and spiritually.

73
00:07:07.347 --> 00:07:11.031
He was a very dangerous man indeed.

